s="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Previous&nbsp;Procedures</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5083 is located at what was previously known as █████ Inc. which is under a facility wide lock down. No personnel below level three clearance may enter the facility without appropriate level three supervision. A tether attached to the elevator and under lock and key must be secured to all D-Class used in testing to avoid escape attempts.</p> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Incident-5083-A Report:</strong> Dr. Spencer was never found, and therefore the task of locating Dr. Spencer has been given the utmost priority. Should Dr. Spencer be found, he is to be contained in a standard human containment cell and administered a Class A Amnestic.</p> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px;"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5083/Dr._R_Spencer_File.jpg" style="width:300px;" alt="Dr._R_Spencer_File.jpg" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:300px;"> <p>On file image of Dr. R. Spencer, if a man fitting this description is seen report findings to O-5 Command immediately.</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Procedures Following Incident 5083-A:</strong> Following the unauthorized use of SCP-5083, no personnel below level four clearance are allowed in the same building as SCP-5083. All requests to experiment with SCP-5083 are to be denied. Anyone who uses the elevator without level five clearance is to be suspended of duty.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5083 is a 1.6 x 2.1 meter elevator and 2 x 30 meter elevator shaft. The elevator is comprised of steel and has seven buttons on the inside of it. The shaft however, is comprised of steel and an unknown substance. SCP-5083 functions as a normal elevator but when button seven is pressed the person(s) inside the elevator will be taken to the place they subconsciously most desire. This function is automatic and does not require user input. Places recorded have been The Fiji Islands, low Earth orbit, and England. In all instances, the elevator returns within 20 minutes after leaving the facility area.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Restricted&nbsp;Logs</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Access&nbsp;Granted</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><em>Included is are Journal entries by Dr. Spencer prior to the day of disappearance</em></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Test 1</strong></p> <p>Test Subject: D-6496 and one camera</p> <p>Foreword: Has a slowly deteriorating mental state. Was a farmer before he was sent to prison. Would often refer to a location he called &quot;the fields&quot;.</p> <p>Location: The elevator arrived in Illinois, in an area commonly used for corn fields.</p> <p>Dr. Spencer: Hey the camera feed is pretty bad, what's going on?</p> <p>D-6496: I-I'm home! HAHA, I'M HOME! Thank you so much I haven't seen sunlight in months!</p> <p>S: You're welcome 6496 but you aren't there to relax and have fun. Tell me what your surroundings look like.</p> <p>6496: I'm in a field, it looks like a farm, I can see some animals in the distance.</p> <p>S: Okay that would make sense, the GPS I attached to the elevator says you are somewhere in Illinois and there is lots of farmland located there.</p> <p>S: It's going to be about time to come back soon, why don't you relax and get some fresh air. Your cooperation at the foundation earned it.</p> <p>[D-6496 spent the next 15 minutes reading in the sunlight]</p> <p>Results: D-6496 seemed to be in a lot better state than he was when he left. He showed much gratitude to personnel for the inclusion of him in the testing of SCP-5083.</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Dr. Spencer's Diary</strong></p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Day 102</span></p> <p><em>It's been a long time here working at the foundation. I feel like I'm a prisoner here, and I'm not even a D-Class! All we do here is kill humans, there's no point, I'm sick of it. I want to use this new SCP I got assigned to, SCP-5083, to get the hell out of here.</em></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Test 2</strong></p> <p>Test Subject: D-7586<br /> <br /> Foreword: Always talked about the 1969 Moon landing. D-7586's Father was an engineer for NASA.</p> <p>Location: The elevator's GPS location was listed as, &quot;unknown&quot;.</p> <p>Dr Spencer: Hey 7586 you there? I can't track you.</p> <p>[Despite contact being tried multiple times it was unsuccessful]</p> <p>Results: D-7586 appeared to have died of asphyxiation, presumably from being subjected to outer space.</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Dr. Spencer's Diary</strong></p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Day 103</span></p> <p><em>Well today was not that great. While I was doing research on the new SCP one of the D-Class was killed. I want to get out of here but I do not want to end up like that. I don't know where I most desire to go, just somewhere far away from here. I need to do more research on this anomaly and myself.</em></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Test 3</strong></p> <p>Test Subject: D-4576</p> <p>Foreword: D-4576 once had a significant interest in surfing. She lived on a beach prior to becoming D-Class. She has been cooperative thus far.</p> <p>Location: The elevator arrived at Kauai Beach.</p> <p>Dr. Spencer: I'm told your at a beach is that correct?</p> <p>D-4576: Ya got that right doc! To bad this tether isn't any longer I could get in the water.</p> <p>S: Yeah well we can't have you escaping on us now would we?</p> <p>4576: Why am I in here anyway? The foundation that is?</p> <p>S: Well&#8230;There could be many different reasons, I'm not to sure, you'd have to pull up your file at &gt;O-5 Council.</p> <p>4576: Ah, well I suppose I just gotta deal with don't I?</p> <p>S: Yeah, one day at a time<br /> Results: D-4576 was covered in sand and even brought back some shells from the beach. Of course those items had to confiscated in case of anomalous properties present.</p> </blockquote> <p><strong>Dr. Spencer's Diary</strong></p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Day 104</span></p> <p><em>I think I'm ready. I'm over this facility. I have to worry about a containment breach and death every day. I can't let my guard down otherwise I will die. My mental state is deteriorating at an extremely fast level, and if I don't do something soon I will kill myself. I am leaving tonight. I pulled up D-4576's file and realized she was one of the lucky few who were taken out of civilian populations. She doesn't deserve to be here. I'm going to take her with me.</em></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Test 4 [UNAUTHORIZED]</strong><br /> Test Subject: Dr. Spencer</p> <p>Foreword: I AM DONE! FUCK THE FACILITY. I AM LEAVING THIS PLACE BEFORE I GET KILLED BY SOME <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/scp-939">LIZARD THAT SPEAKS</a>.</p> <p>Location: Jubgᘿᓰᘺᖽᐸᕼஜ۩۞۩ஜ𝑒Ⓘʷ𝔨ｈஜ۩۞۩ஜ</p> <p>Results:</p> </blockquote> <p>After 10/21/2019, Dr. R. Spencer level four personnel and D-4576-R(ouge) level one personnel are considered high priority for capture and containment. Any information on there whereabouts will be met with a large reward.</p> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hawkillo" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5340588&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606099687" alt="Hawkillo" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5340588)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/hawkillo" >Hawkillo</a></span></p> 
